# The backlog is the database, and runs.log is the only record that contains failed runs.
#
# The root .gitignore excludes *.log, which silently swallowed every ticket's runs.log — so the
# file DECISIONS.md cites as authoritative for cost ("about $165 ... summed from runs.log", M1
# closing entry) and for the runs missing from ticket.md's history ("runs.log has them") existed
# on one laptop and in no clone. A ticket folder without it understates what the ticket cost and
# loses every run that failed.
#
# Patterns in a lower-level .gitignore override a parent's, so this re-includes them. It lives
# here rather than as a negation in the root file deliberately: nothing outside backlog/ needs to
# know, and the rule sits next to the data it protects.
!runs.log
